# InfoMapper Development Rules

## Code walktrough

- Check the code exactly, never hipothesize

## Architecture Patterns

- Follow layered architecture: Domain → Projection → UI → Sources
- Use command pattern for state mutations (lib/commands.ts)
- Never modify store state directly - always use command functions
- Use projection functions to transform domain models to UI views

## Component Standards

- Follow naming convention: `type_object_context` (see docs/INFOMAPPER_COMPONENT_REFERENCE_v1.0.md)
- Use `im-*` prefix for custom UI components (im-button, im-input, etc.)
- Maintain 28px control height for consistency
- Use 12px base font size, 10px for data types, 14px for headings

## TypeScript Requirements

- Strict mode enabled - no `any` types
- Explicit return types for all functions
- Use proper types from lib/types.ts and lib/source-types.ts

## ID Generation

- Use lib/id.ts utilities for generating IDs
- Follow pattern: `{prefix}_{timestamp}{random}`
- Never create IDs manually

## Error Handling

- Use centralized error-handler.ts
- Show user-friendly toast notifications
- Handle localStorage failures gracefully

